import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 283 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: The Tang-Luo System's Internal Logic","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 283 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: The Tang-Luo System's Internal Logic","no":283,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Setting Self-Consistency","Internal Logic","System Assessment","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","99-Document Version and Maintenance Notes"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0283_模块2-唐罗-设定自洽度评估.md","filePath":"en/0283_模块2-唐罗-设定自洽度评估.md"}`),o={name:"en/0283_模块2-唐罗-设定自洽度评估.md"};function a(r,e,l,c,h,u){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-283-tang-luo-decomposition-setting-self-consistency-assessment-the-tang-luo-system-s-internal-logic" tabindex="-1">Entry 283 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: The Tang-Luo System&#39;s Internal Logic <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-283-tang-luo-decomposition-setting-self-consistency-assessment-the-tang-luo-system-s-internal-logic" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 283 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: The Tang-Luo System&#39;s Internal Logic&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 33)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-within-the-tang-luo-system-can-the-logic-be-self-consistent" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Within the Tang-Luo system, can the logic be self-consistent <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-within-the-tang-luo-system-can-the-logic-be-self-consistent" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Within the Tang-Luo system, can the logic be self-consistent&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom requires setting self-consistency over plot convenience. The sixth segment in the first six-segment structure — setting self-consistency / retcon-ending risk assessment — receives special expansion in this entry. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, systematically assessing the Tang-Luo system&#39;s internal logical self-consistency. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Insufficient self-consistency&#39;s energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Patch cost</strong>: because internal logic occasionally has holes, the author must continuously patch. Patching itself consumes creative energy</li><li><strong>Reader confusion</strong>: settings not self-consistent, readers will be confused, question, abandon the book. Confusion itself is civilization-level narrative waste</li><li><strong>Expansion constrained</strong>: because underlying logic has holes, world-view expansion must be cautious, otherwise old holes are amplified by new content</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-self-consistency-perspective" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Self-Consistency Perspective) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-self-consistency-perspective" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Self-Consistency Perspective)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Regression caused by insufficient setting self-consistency:</p><ol><li><strong>Rule drift</strong>: because underlying logic is not hard, rules drift with plot. Readers gradually stop believing these rules</li><li><strong>Explanation cost</strong>: every rule drift requires the author to spend large space explaining. Explanation replaces narrative, story becomes hard to read</li><li><strong>Trust collapse</strong>: once readers discover rules can be arbitrarily modified, they stop immersing. Narrative&#39;s foundation — &quot;believing in this world&quot; — collapses</li></ol><p>Regression form: not civilization regression, but narrative regression — readers no longer believe the world the author tells.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking behind insufficient self-consistency:</p><ul><li><strong>Convenience first</strong>: for plot convenience, the author may sacrifice setting self-consistency. This is predation on reader trust</li><li><strong>Protagonist halo</strong>: if settings cannot be self-consistent, use &quot;protagonist halo&quot; to brush off. The halo is predation on laws</li><li><strong>Number padding</strong>: to let the protagonist continue leveling, early iron laws are torn. This is predation on the numerical ladder early-built with effort</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Self-Consistency Medium-High</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Self-Consistency High</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rules occasionally drift</td><td>Laws first, rules do not drift</td></tr><tr><td>Patch-style maintenance</td><td>Law-first, no patch needed</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist halo backstop</td><td>Law-anchored, no halo concept</td></tr><tr><td>Expansion constrained</td><td>Can expand infinitely without collapse</td></tr><tr><td>Trust fragile</td><td>Trust stable</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Tang-Luo system&#39;s self-consistency score: <strong>medium-high</strong>. Its realm system, academy rules are largely self-consistent within the world-view; no Douluo-style late padding or Shrouding-the-Heavens-style realm collapse is seen. But self-consistency highly depends on the premise that &quot;Tang Luo himself is always in office&quot;; once plot requires him to leave, rules hang in the air.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: fully replicate Tang-Luo system rules</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Tang Luo leaves&quot; plot shock</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: number of rule-hanging points, positions needing patches</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: rule-hanging points concentrate in three places — &quot;top-tier knowledge,&quot; &quot;resource distribution,&quot; &quot;adjudication right&quot; — precisely the structural defects repeatedly pointed out in the first 32 entries of this series</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong> (consistent with Entry 251 overview)</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong></li><li><strong>Risk-point positioning</strong>: top-tier knowledge private, racial narrowness, single-point dependency — these three places if plot-shocked, must retcon</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: patch cost and reader-confusion cost</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: convenience first = predation on reader trust</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo self-consistency medium-high, main risk in single-point dependency</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: self-consistency must cover 99% beings&#39; situations, not only the protagonist</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: infinitely expandable self-consistency is the precondition for cross-plane</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-discussion-network-verification-of-internal-logic" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Discussion: Network Verification of Internal Logic <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-discussion-network-verification-of-internal-logic" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Discussion: Network Verification of Internal Logic&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang-Luo system&#39;s setting self-consistency is judged medium self-consistent after Alaya Network&#39;s formal verification — it can explain itself but many places rely on protagonist halo to fill cracks. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s law-first axiom requires any setting to pass logical self-consistency verification in the law network, not rely on plot patch-up. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s self-consistency standard is higher: not only internally contradiction-free, but also compatible with Myriad Races republicanism, the universal equal infinite law, and other underlying axioms. The Tang-Luo system&#39;s logical holes have nowhere to hide in network verification.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang-Luo system&#39;s self-consistency is above-average among traditional web novels — it at least has no Douluo-style number padding, nor Shrouding-the-Heavens-style realm collapse. But its self-consistency is &quot;person present = self-consistent&quot;; once the person retires, it leaks. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s requirement is &quot;law present = self-consistent&quot;; any individual exits, self-consistency does not drop.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · setting self-consistency assessment described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a> · <a href="./14-修炼境界统一划分.html">14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification</a> · <a href="./99-文档版本与维护说明.html">99-Document Version and Maintenance Notes</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=t(o,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
